REMARK   1 DENGUE-2 NS1 DIRECTION B EPITOPE (PRIMARY) — RFantibody TARGET
REMARK   2 
REMARK   3 PDB DESCRIPTION:
REMARK   3   Source: PDB 7K93 (DENV-2 NS1 in complex with 2B7 antibody, X-ray 2.89 Å, deposited 2020)
REMARK   3   Chain: T (relabeled from chain A for RFantibody compatibility)
REMARK   3   Structure: Partial β-ladder-enriched fragment
REMARK   3   CA residues: 146 total (residues 23-346 in PDB numbering, heavily gapped)
REMARK   3   Target epitope: Direction B (PRIMARY target; rigid β-ladder patch, residues ~261–305)
REMARK   3 
REMARK   4 EPITOPE DEFINITION:
REMARK   4   Patch: rigid β-ladder region (~residues 261–305, the hydrophobic core of the β-sandwich)
REMARK   4   Conserved across DENV1–4; avoids the tip region (~311–352, host mimicry / false-positive risk)
REMARK   4   Rationale: structural rigidity (higher designability than the disordered wing/connector)
REMARK   4 
REMARK   5 VALIDATION:
REMARK   5   Status: Two variant patches tested in de-novo minibinder pilots
REMARK   5   (1) P1 (charged, residues 269–296): 0/200 designs pass (ipTM max 0.11, pAE min 27.8 Å)
REMARK   5   (2) P2 (hydrophobic, residues 282–289): 0/200 designs pass (ipTM max 0.11, pAE min 27.7 Å)
REMARK   5   Geometry: flat β-sheet surface (mean curvature ~0, no significant concavity)
REMARK   5   Conclusion: Direction B is flat-to-convex; de-novo binding requires pocket (not present here)
REMARK   5 
REMARK   6 RFdiffusion PARAMETERS (tested on de-novo minibinders; RFantibody nanobodies untested):
REMARK   6   VHH framework: h-NbBCII10 (if pursuing RFantibody variant)
REMARK   6   Design loops: H1:7, H2:6, H3:5–13
REMARK   6   Diffusion timesteps: 50
REMARK   6   Validation: RF2_ab (10 recycles) or AlphaFold2-multimer
REMARK   6 
REMARK   7 CAVEATS & RATIONALE FOR DIRECTION C:
REMARK   7   Direction B is the PROJECT'S PRIMARY target (stated in brief) for its rigidity.
REMARK   7   However, de-novo minibinders failed comprehensively (400 designs, 0% pass).
REMARK   7   The β-ladder is a flat surface with minimal curvature; RFdiffusion de-novo requires
REMARK   7   a concave pocket to grip. Direction C (connector patch) is more concave (158.8 atoms
REMARK   7   within 10 Å vs 135.6 for the β-ladder) and yielded better pilot nanobody metrics
REMARK   7   (interaction_pAE 16–17 Å, closer to passing <5 Å threshold).
REMARK   7   DECISION: Active path is Direction C (Option 1). Direction B is archived as
REMARK   7   documented hard case. (Both are DENV-specific, pan-serotype conserved.)
REMARK   8 
REMARK   9 HISTORY:
REMARK   9   Created: 2026-07-19 (backup target; active path is Direction C)
REMARK   9   Purpose: RFantibody nanobody design (de-novo minibinder route exhausted)
REMARK   9   Status: Direction C prioritized for higher expected pass rate
REMARK   9 
